      <ul>
        <li>No employer letter needed—bank statements and invoices prove freelance income</li>
        <li>Earn above the SMI threshold (€1,445/month, ~€17,340/year) with documented, consistent income</li>
        <li>Provide 3–6 months of bank statements and matching invoices to consulate</li>
        <li>Register as autónomo within 30 days of arrival; costs ~€300–€350/month in social contributions</li>
        <li>Eligible for Beckham Law (24% flat tax) once you become a Spanish tax resident</li>
        <li>File quarterly VAT and annual income tax returns in Spain</li>
        <li>Verify your home country's tax requirements independently</li>
        <li>Professional documentation (website, contracts, invoices) strengthens your application</li>
        <li>Multiple small clients are better than one large client for perceived income stability</li>
